course: dictionary
lesson: 569
title: Animals from long ago
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An aurochs was a huge wild ox with long horns. You can work this out from the sentence: «All cattle come from the aurochs, a huge wild ox with long horns drawn in cave paintings.» The words after the comma explain what an aurochs was, so the clues are huge, wild and horned.
explain: The clues can also tell you about time. «The last one died in a Polish forest in 1627.» This means no aurochs were alive after that year. Extinct means that every animal of a kind has died out, so the aurochs became extinct in 1627.
explain: Notice the two words after the first sentence in the example: «it was tamed about 10,000 years ago». Tamed means people trained the wild animal to live with them. Today's farm cows are the tamed descendants of the aurochs, so when you read about a long-gone animal, look for clues about how it changed or disappeared.
fact: An aurochs was a huge wild ox with long horns.
fact: Aurochs lived in Europe, Asia and North Africa.
fact: The last aurochs died in a Polish forest in 1627.
fact: «Extinct» means that every animal of its kind has died out.
fact: Today's cattle are descended from the aurochs; people tamed them about 10,000 years ago.
exercise: «All cattle come from the aurochs, a huge wild ox with long horns.» What is an aurochs? | A wild bird with long legs | A kind of farm tractor | A small pet rabbit | *A huge wild ox with long horns
exercise: «The last one died in a Polish forest in 1627.» What does this tell you about aurochs today? | *There are none left alive | There are many of them in Polish forests | They have been tamed and live on farms | They only live in Asia
exercise: «The aurochs became extinct in 1627.» What does extinct mean? | *No longer alive anywhere | Very rare, but still living in the woods | Hiding from hunters | Moved to a new country
test: «Aurochs are drawn in cave paintings like those at Lascaux.» Where were aurochs shown, according to this sentence? | On farm tractors | In cave paintings | In city parks | *In cave paintings, like those at Lascaux
test: Farm cows are the tamed descendants of the aurochs. What does tamed mean here? | Hunted to extinction | Made very big and strong | Painted on cave walls | *Trained to live with people
exam: «The aurochs became extinct because of hunting and loss of land.» What does loss of land suggest? | They were tamed and moved to farms | They had too many children | *Their homes were taken away, so there was less space for them | They were given more land to live on
